      {
         "id": "b",
         "prompt": "Use your answer to part (a) to find \\( f(2) \\), and use separation of variables to find \\( f(t) \\) for \\( t \\ge 2 \\).",
         "setup_required": false,
         "answer_latex": "f(t) = \\frac{100}{t^{2}}",
         "worked_solution": [
            {
               "text": "By continuity, the second equation starts from the value the first solution reaches.",
               "latex": "f(2) = (4 + 1)^{2} = 25"
            },
            {
               "text": "Separate the variables.",
               "latex": "\\frac{1}{y}\\,dy = -\\frac{2}{t}\\,dt"
            },
            {
               "text": "Antidifferentiate both sides.",
               "latex": "\\ln|y| = -2\\ln t + C"
            },
            {
               "text": "Since y is positive, y = A/t^2 with A = e^C, and f(2) = 25 gives A = 100.",
               "latex": "25 = \\frac{A}{4}, \\quad A = 100"
            },
            {
               "text": "State the solution.",
               "latex": "f(t) = \\frac{100}{t^{2}}"
            }
         ],
