      {
         "id": "c",
         "prompt": "Let \\( W \\) be the function with \\( W'(t) = f(t) \\) for \\( t \\ge 0 \\) and \\( W(0) = 10 \\). Find \\( W(4) \\).",
         "setup_required": false,
         "answer_latex": "W(4) = \\frac{731}{15}",
         "worked_solution": [
            {
               "text": "Start from W(0) and add the accumulated change, split where the formula for f changes.",
               "latex": "W(4) = 10 + \\int_{0}^{2} (t^{2}+1)^{2}\\,dt + \\int_{2}^{4} \\frac{100}{t^{2}}\\,dt"
            },
            {
               "text": "First integral.",
               "latex": "\\int_{0}^{2} (t^{4} + 2t^{2} + 1)\\,dt = \\frac{32}{5} + \\frac{16}{3} + 2 = \\frac{206}{15}"
            },
            {
               "text": "Second integral.",
               "latex": "\\int_{2}^{4} \\frac{100}{t^{2}}\\,dt = 100\\left(\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{1}{4}\\right) = 25"
            },
            {
               "text": "Add.",
               "latex": "W(4) = 10 + \\frac{206}{15} + 25 = \\frac{731}{15}"
            }
         ],
